<h1 id=3D"F215343:Rx:Enabler-CorrectRXAccessforCarved-outMembers-_Toc207888=
643Scenarios"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"F215343:Rx:Enabl=
er-CorrectRXAccessforCarved-outMembers-_Toc207888643"><span class=3D"conflu=
ence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc207888643"></span></span>Scenarios</h1>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Prescription claim with fillDate before coverage effectiveStart =E2=86=
=92 excluded from both list and detail.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Refill order straddling effective window (e.g., refill date before effec=
tiveStart, claim date within) =E2=86=92 excluded.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Refill request with refillsLeft =3D 0 =E2=86=92 disallowed with clear me=
ssage.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Member without attestation (CVSRxCarveOut =3D false) =E2=86=92 UI shows =
link-out, not embedded services.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Missing startDate/endDate query parameters =E2=86=92 service throws 400 =
Bad Request.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Claims flagged as sensitive (isSensitive=3Dtrue) =E2=86=92 excluded if U=
AF rules deny visibility.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Dependent under 18 without family access rules =E2=86=92 excluded unless=
 explicitly authorized.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Duplicate claims with same uniqueRxId =E2=86=92 keep only claim with lat=
est fillDate.</p></li>
</ol>
<h1 id=3D"F215343:Rx:Enabler-CorrectRXAccessforCarved-outMembers-API&amp;Sw=
agger(PharmacyServicev1)">API &amp; Swagger (Pharmacy Service v1)</h1>
<h2 id=3D"F215343:Rx:Enabler-CorrectRXAccessforCarved-outMembers-Acquisitio=
n&amp;FilteringModes(Explicit)">Acquisition &amp; Filtering Modes (Explicit=
)</h2>
<p>The Pharmacy Service supports two integration modes, both enforcing the =
same Policy Effective Window, attestation, UAF privacy, family access rules=
, and deduplication by uniqueRxId. Choose the mode based on where claims ar=
e acquired.</p>
<h3 id=3D"F215343:Rx:Enabler-CorrectRXAccessforCarved-outMembers-ModeA=E2=
=80=94Servicefetch-and-filter(recommendedforPLP/PDB,PlaceOrder,ShipConsent,=
i90)">Mode A =E2=80=94 Service fetch-and-filter (recommended for PLP/PDB, P=
laceOrder, Ship Consent, i90)</h3>
<p>=E2=80=A2 Call POST /v1/prescriptions/search (and GET /v1/prescriptions/=
{claimId} for detail).</p>
<p>=E2=80=A2 Service obtains CVS Auth (patient profile token), calls Consol=
idated Claims (/getClaimsHistory), then normalizes, deduplicates (uniqueRxI=
d, keep latest fillDate), and applies the Policy Effective Window =3D [phar=
macy membership effectiveStart/effectiveEnd] =E2=88=A9 [request startDate/e=
ndDate].</p>
<p>=E2=80=A2 UAF privacy and family access are applied; attestation (CVSRxC=
arveOut) gates embedded capabilities.</p>
<p>=E2=80=A2 Partial results: HTTP 200 with additional_data.code=3DPARTIAL_=
SUCCESS by default, or opt-in HTTP 206 via Prefer: partial=3D206 or partial=
As=3D206.</p>
<h3 id=3D"F215343:Rx:Enabler-CorrectRXAccessforCarved-outMembers-ModeB=E2=
=80=94Filter-only(callerpassesrawclaims;usedbynewstories/ETL/reviewqueues)"=
>Mode B =E2=80=94 Filter-only (caller passes raw claims; used by new storie=
s/ETL/review queues)</h3>
<p>=E2=80=A2 Call POST /v1/visibility/evaluate with claims[].</p>
<p>=E2=80=A2 Service treats inputs as the source of truth for items to eval=
uate and applies the same policy stack: effective window, UAF privacy, fami=
ly access, and dedup.</p>
<p>=E2=80=A2 Returns decisions[] plus a normalized PrescriptionSummary for =
visible items.</p>
<p>=E2=80=A2 Partial results semantics identical to Mode A (200 default, or=
 206 with headers on opt-in).</p>
<h2 id=3D"F215343:Rx:Enabler-CorrectRXAccessforCarved-outMembers-Overview">=
Overview</h2>
<p>This section defines the authoritative API contract for the Pharmacy Ser=
vice enforcing the Policy Effective Window Filter across list, detail, and =
generic visibility use cases. All routes are prefixed with /v1. The full Op=
enAPI 3.0.3 specification is attached separately; this section provides a c=
oncise summary and examples.</p>
<p>Endpoints (v1):</p>
<p>=E2=80=A2 GET /v1/health =E2=80=93 service probe</p>
<p>=E2=80=A2 GET /v1/coverage/windows =E2=80=93 resolve Aetna-aligned effec=
tive coverage windows for one or more members</p>
<p>=E2=80=A2 POST /v1/prescriptions/search =E2=80=93 authoritative list (wi=
ndow trim, privacy/family access, dedup)</p>
<p>=E2=80=A2 GET /v1/prescriptions/{claimId} =E2=80=93 authoritative detail=
 view</p>
<p>=E2=80=A2 POST /v1/visibility/evaluate =E2=80=93 generic batch evaluator=
 for new/adjacent use cases</p>
<h2 id=3D"F215343:Rx:Enabler-CorrectRXAccessforCarved-outMembers-Versioning=
&amp;Stability">Versioning &amp; Stability</h2>
<p>All endpoints are versioned under /v1. Breaking changes will result in a=
 new major prefix (/v2). Non-breaking, additive fields are gated via tolera=
nt readers and do not change the version path.</p>
<h2 id=3D"F215343:Rx:Enabler-CorrectRXAccessforCarved-outMembers-ErrorModel=
&amp;FailureIDs">Error Model &amp; Failure IDs</h2>
<p>Responses are wrapped in a standard envelope. For errors (4xx/5xx), the =
API returns an ErrorEnvelope with additional_data carrying canonical failur=
e identifiers and reasons. These are suitable for telemetry and client-side=
 branching.</p>
<p>Common failure_id values:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>MISSING_REQUIRED_DATE =E2=80=93 startDate and/or endDate missing</p></li=
>
<li>
<p>INVALID_DATE_FORMAT =E2=80=93 dates not ISO YYYY-MM-DD</p></li>
<li>
<p>INVALID_DATE_RANGE =E2=80=93 startDate after endDate</p></li>
<li>
<p>NOT_ATTESTED =E2=80=93 embedded capabilities disallowed by attestation</=
p></li>
<li>
<p>CLAIM_NOT_FOUND =E2=80=93 claimId not associated to visible member</p></=
li>
<li>
<p>CLAIM_OUTSIDE_EFFECTIVE_WINDOW =E2=80=93 claim exists but fillDate outsi=
de effective window</p></li>
<li>
<p>HIDDEN_BY_PRIVACY / HIDDEN_BY_FAMILY_ACCESS =E2=80=93 filtered by UAF/fa=
mily rules</p></li>
<li>
<p>INVALID_MEMBERSHIP_ID =E2=80=93 malformed membershipResourceId</p></li>
<li>
<p>TOKEN_EXPIRED / UPSTREAM_UNAVAILABLE =E2=80=93 dependency failures</p></=
li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"F215343:Rx:Enabler-CorrectRXAccessforCarved-outMembers-PartialRes=
ultsSemantics(200vs206)">Partial Results Semantics (200 vs 206)</h2>
<p>When a list/batch contains a mix of eligible and ineligible items, the A=
PI does not fail the request. By default it returns HTTP 200 with additiona=
l_data.code=3DPARTIAL_SUCCESS, placing only eligible items in data and capt=
uring excluded items under additional_data.partial_failures[].</p>
<p>Clients can opt into explicit partial semantics via either:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Header: Prefer: partial=3D206</p></li>
<li>
<p>Query: partialAs=3D206</p></li>
</ul>
<p>When used, the service responds with HTTP 206 and includes headers X-Par=
tial-Result=3Dtrue and X-Partial-Reason.</p>
<h2 id=3D"F215343:Rx:Enabler-CorrectRXAccessforCarved-outMembers-BriefExamp=
les">Brief Examples</h2>
<p>POST /v1/prescriptions/search?startDate=3D2019-01-01&amp;endDate=3D2019-=
12-31</p>
<p>Request body (subset):</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">{
  "membershipResourceIds": [
    "5~263801696+31+1+20180101+788678+C+3"
  ],
  "options": {
    "applyPrivacy": true,
    "applyFamilyAccess": true,
    "applyDeduplication": true,
    "requireAttestation": true
  }
}</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>Response 200 (partial success, truncated):</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">{
    "statusCode": 200,
    "statusDescription": "OK",
    "additional_data": {
      "code": "PARTIAL_SUCCESS",
      "partial": true,
      "counts": {"total": 2, "eligible": 1, "hiddenByEffectiveWindow": 1},
      "partial_failures": [{
        "failure_id": "CLAIM_OUTSIDE_EFFECTIVE_WINDOW",
        "diagnostics": {"claimId": "200023611694002", "fillDate": "2018-04-=
12"}
      }]
    },
    "data": [{
      "membershipResourceId": "5~263801696+31+1+20180101+788678+C+3",
      "prescriptionList": [{"claimId": "200023611694001", "drugName": "Lipi=
tor", "lastFilledDate": "2019-08-12"}]
    }]
}</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>POST /v1/visibility/evaluate?startDate=3D2019-01-01&amp;endDate=3D2019-1=
2-31&amp;partialAs=3D206 (client opts into 206)</p>
<p>Response 206 (partial content, truncated):</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">{
    "statusCode": 200,
    "statusDescription": "OK",
    "additional_data": {"code": "PARTIAL_SUCCESS", "partial": true},
    "data": {"decisions": [{"claimNumber": "200023611694001", "visibility":=
 "eligible"}]}
}</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>Headers: X-Partial-Result: true; X-Partial-Reason: CLAIM_OUTSIDE_EFFECTI=
VE_WINDOW</p>
<h2 id=3D"F215343:Rx:Enabler-CorrectRXAccessforCarved-outMembers-Artifacts"=
>Artifacts</h2>
<p>=E2=80=A2 OpenAPI 3.0.3: pharmacy-service-v1d.yaml</p>
<p>=E2=80=A2 Postman: pharmacy-service.postman_collection.v2.json, pharmacy=
-service.postman_environment.json</p>
<p>=E2=80=A2 Client stubs: pharmacy-service-client-stubs.ts</p>
<p><br></p>
<h1 id=3D"F215343:Rx:Enabler-CorrectRXAccessforCarved-outMembers-_Toc207888=
645Services(Expanded)"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"F215343=
:Rx:Enabler-CorrectRXAccessforCarved-outMembers-_Toc207888645"><span class=
=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc207888645"></span></span>Services (Ex=
panded)</h1>
<p>Below are the core services and their interactions, expanded with field-=
level mappings and sample payloads to ensure precise architectural alignmen=
t.</p>
<p>=E2=80=A2 CVS Auth Service (`GET /cvs_auth_token_data`): issues token wi=
th member demographics and identifiers.</p>
<p>=E2=80=A2 Consolidated Claims Service (`GET /pharmacyclaims`): retrieves=
 raw claim history across visible plan members.</p>
<p>=E2=80=A2 Prescription List Service (`POST /prescriptions/search`): appl=
ies filtering, deduplication, effective date window.</p>
<p>=E2=80=A2 Prescription Detail Service (`GET /prescriptions?claimId=3D=E2=
=80=A6`): enriches a single prescription with dosage, refills, cost.</p>
<p>=E2=80=A2 Order &amp; Refill Service: manages refill eligibility and ord=
er placement with effective date enforcement.</p>
<p>=E2=80=A2 Family Access Rules (`/familyaccessrules`): ensures dependent =
entitlements are respected.</p>
<p>=E2=80=A2 UAF Service: privacy restrictions enforced per member and medi=
cation.</p>
<p>=E2=80=A2 Centralized Eligibility Middleware: authoritative Policy Effec=
tive Window enforcement.</p>
<h1 id=3D"F215343:Rx:Enabler-CorrectRXAccessforCarved-outMembers-_Toc207888=
646Appendix:SwaggerSummary(PharmacyServicev1)"><span class=3D"confluence-an=
